Who we are

Conclusion Lifecycl e
is the Managed Services brand of Conclusion Iberia, focused on delivering long-term, scalable IT services across the full lifecycle, from build to run.
It brings together the Managed Services operation that was previously part of Neotalent Conclusion, with a clearer focus on lifecycle ownership, operational excellence, and long-term partnerships.

Conclusion Lifecycle also acts as the incubator for new lifecycle-based service offerings within Conclusion Iberia, supporting clients with sustainable, resilient, and continuously evolving digital solutions.

Find out more about us at Conclusion Lifecycle.

Role Overview

We are looking for an AI Integrations Developer (.NET / Azure AI) to join one of our Nearshore Teams working remotely for international clients accross The Netherlands, Germany and other European countries.
This role combines hands-on AI implementation with strong integration engineering, focusing on connecting AI services, enterprise applications, and data sources into scalable, production-ready ecosystems.
You will play a key role in building AI-powered applications, speech-to-text solutions, and generative AI use cases, while ensuring seamless integration with internal and external systems through modern API-driven architectures.

What you will do

Develop and maintain AI-powered applications using .NET, C#, Azure AI services, and modern cloud technologies;
Implement generative AI solutions for summarisation, information extraction, classification, intelligent search, and automation scenarios;
Build and support speech-to-text and transcription pipelines using Azure Speech Services, Whisper-based technologies, and related AI services;
Design, develop, and maintain integrations through REST and SOAP APIs, connecting AI solutions with enterprise systems, third-party platforms, and business data sources;
Contribute to Azure-based solutions, including Azure Functions, API Management, Azure DevOps, CI/CD pipelines, and cloud-native application development practices;
Ensure quality, reliability, and maintainability through testing, monitoring, documentation, and Agile delivery practices.

What you are like

Proficient in .NET / C# development, including .NET Core and modern .NET versions, with experience building APIs, backend services, and orchestration layers;
Experienced in applying AI technologies in production environments, including Azure OpenAI, GPT-based models, RAG architectures, AI search, and speech-to-text solutions;
Strong background in system integration, with proven expertise in REST and SOAP APIs and connecting disparate enterprise systems;
Comfortable working with Azure services such as Azure Functions, API Management, Azure DevOps, and CI/CD pipelines;
Proficient in SQL Server and familiar with NoSQL databases such as Cosmos DB and/or MongoDB; Oracle knowledge is valued;
Experienced with software quality practices, including NUnit, FluentAssertions, Postman, Git, Agile, and Scrum methodologies;
Strong written and spoken English skills, with the ability to communicate effectively with both technical and business stakeholders;
Familiarity with Python, microservices, Microsoft Graph, SharePoint integrations, and Azure or AI-related certifications is considered a plus;
Regular user of AI-assisted development tools such as GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Claude Code, Codex, or similar solutions;
Proactive, pragmatic, and hands-on, with a strong focus on delivering business value through both AI implementation and enterprise integration.

Why join us

Work on challenging projects for big clients;
Learn more about emerging technologies;
Possibility of working remotely;
Design your career plan;
Access to continuous training and certifications;
Evolve through our internal mobility program;
… and much more!

